:: Blackmail Letter
<<set $xchange.blackmail.cooldown to 7>>
<<set _blackmailReturn to $phase is 2 ? "Bird Tower" : $phase is 3 ? "Wolf Cave" : $phase is 4 ? "Temple" : $phase is 5 ? "Mansion Bedroom" : "Bedroom">>
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 0>>
	<<if $phase is 1>>You spotted this strange envelope lying by the door. <</if>>Curious, you turn it over in your hands, feeling its shape and weight.
	<br><br>
	It's addressed to you by name, yet has no address written down.
	<<if $phase is 0 or $phase is 1>>
		It must have been delivered personally to the orphanage.
	<<else>>
		Whoever brought it must have delivered it personally.
	<</if>>
	The name seems written hastily, or at least it pretends to give off that impression. It's sealed tight, showing no signs of tampering. It seems intended for your eyes only.
	<br><br>
	Without further ado, you open it up and fetch the letter inside. It reads:
	<p class="indent-block italic">
		"Greetings, <<underworld_nickname>>.
		<br><br> 
		We've come into posession of some titilating pictures of your pretty little self with the help of some of our contacts and colaborators. And we've come to believe that it would be an incredible waste to let go of the sweet potential that a body like yours offers. 
		<br><br>
		Please refer to the pictures included within this envelope, so that we can reach an understanding of what this communication entails."
	</p>
	You're starting to get weirded out by such a strangely worded letter, but nevertheless feel compelled to check the contents of the envelope.
	<br><br>	
	<<link [[Look inside|Blackmail Letter Intro 2]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial>>
	There's the dreaded envelope. You don't have to look inside to know what it contains: More blackmail.<br>
	You steel yourself and resolutely open the envelope to find an all too familiar letter.
	<br><br>
	<p class="indent-block italic">
		"Greetings, <<underworld_nickname>>.
		<br><br>
		Wow, you've been naughty since our last communication. People have been talking about you, and more material has been steadily dropping on our laps. We couldn't be happier for your selfless service.
		<br><br>
		However, people from our club have been asking for more. They've been making requests. Requests that we're all too happy to extend onto you.
		<br><br>
		<<if penaltyFameSum() lt 1000 and !$xchange.blackmail.paymentsRemoved>>
			The deal is the same as last time. Indulge our request, and <span class="gold">we'll help with your weekly debt</span>.<br>
			Refuse, and we'll signal-boost whatever stuff is out there. The choice is yours.
		<<else>>
			Please, we hope you'll indulge our humble request willingly.<br>
			But if you refuse, we'll have to signal-boost whatever stuff is out there. The choice is yours.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		Here's your task:
		<<blackmail-newquest>>
		We thank you in advance for your compliance. And may you have fun while doing so.
		<br><br>
		<b>Signed:</b><br>
		<i>The Gentleman's Club</i>"
		<br><br>
	</p>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
	<<if $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.includesItems>>
		<<linkreplace "Take contents">>
			You've taken the included items.
			<<run $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.receiveItems()>>
			<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.includesItems to false>>
			<<updatesidebarimg>>
		<</linkreplace>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link "Close" _blackmailReturn>><<set $xchange.blackmail.hasReadLetter to true>><<if _blackmailReturn isnot "Bedroom">><<endevent>><</if>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	Another envelope this week fitting the usual description of your blackmailer's requests.<br>
	You steel yourself and resolutely open the envelope to find an all too familiar letter.
	<br><br>
	<p class="indent-block italic">
		"Greetings, <<underworld_nickname>>. 
		<br><br>
		<span class="green">People were really pleased with your service last time.</span> So they've been asking us for more.<br>
		And considering how generous you were last week in indulging our request, we are all too happy to mediate their wishes and extend them onto you.
		<br><br>
		If you check the contents of this envelope, you'll find a sample of the material that, in partnership with you, we were able to produce last week." 
		<br><br>
	</p>
	You peek into the contents and, horrified, verify that this is indeed true. Plenty of photos where your flushed body is squarely within view. And even those that do not show your face directly still have a small portrait photo attached to a corner, implying they're still you. 
	<br><br>
	To make matters worse, they've managed to make you look even lewder through skillful use of camera angles. Way worse than if anyone had seen you live. You have no idea how they've accomplished such a feat. 
	<<set _penaltyFameMax to penaltyFameMax()>>
	<<if _penaltyFameMax gte 1000>>
		<span class="red">It would be a complete disaster if these got out.</span>
	<<elseif _penaltyFameMax gt 400>>
		<span class="pink">These would ruin your reputation if they got out.</span>
	<<elseif _penaltyFameMax gt 200>>
		<span class="purple">It would definitely hurt your reputation if these got out.</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="blue">However, you think you may be able to deny them being real.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<p class="indent-block italic">
		<<if penaltyFameSum() lt 1000 and !$xchange.blackmail.paymentsRemoved>>
			"The deal is the same as last time. Indulge our request, and <span class="gold">we'll help with your weekly debt</span>.<br>
			Refuse, and we'll release these into the wild. The choice is yours.
		<<else>>
			"Please, we hope you'll indulge our humble request willingly.<br>
			But if you refuse, we'll be forced to release these into the wild. The choice is yours.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		Here's your task:		
		<<blackmail-newquest>>
		We thank you in advance for your compliance. And may you have fun while doing so.
		<br><br>
		<b>Signed:</b><br>
		<i>The Gentleman's Club</i>"
		<br><br>
	</p>
	<<if $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.includesItems>>
		<<linkreplace "Take contents">>
			You've taken the included items.
			<<run $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.receiveItems()>>
			<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.includesItems to false>>
			<<updatesidebarimg>>
		<</linkreplace>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link "Close" _blackmailReturn>><<set $xchange.blackmail.hasReadLetter to true>><<if _blackmailReturn isnot "Bedroom">><<endevent>><</if>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Blackmail Letter Intro 2
<<set _blackmailReturn to $phase is 2 ? "Bird Tower" : $phase is 3 ? "Wolf Cave" : $phase is 4 ? "Temple" : $phase is 5 ? "Mansion Bedroom" : "Bedroom">>
Within you find the aforementioned pictures. And while looking at them, their horror dawns on you. They display what seems like a disrobed body in very graphic detail. Your body, to be exact. And it looks incredibly lewd.
<br><br>
There's several close-ups on your most intimate areas, and even pictures showing your face squarely within frame. Leaving no doubt to anyone seeing them as to the fact that they indeed are photos of you.
<br><br>
<p class="indent-block italic">
	"Assuming you've already looked at the contents of the envelope, we believe you might already suspect what this letter is all about.
	<br><br>
	We're the proud owners of very discreet and exclusive club, that prides itself on its exquisite taste. And so, you've been chosen as the current subject of our delight. Please understand that what we offer you is not a threat, but an opportunity; as we understand you're currently in financial straits with your caretaker.
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold"><b>Comply</b> with our demands, and we'll help with your weekly debt</span>.<br>
	<span class="purple"><b>Refuse</b>, and we'll regretfully be forced to release this exquisite material out into the world.</span>
	<br><br>
	We hope you'll remain agreeable to this mutually beneficial partnership. <br>
	You may ignore this letter. But should you decide to do so, you should be prepared to suffer the consequences. 
	<br><br>
	Otherwise, we welcome you into our fold. And to celebrate, this is today's task:
	<<blackmail-newquest>>
	We thank you in advance for your compliance. And may you have fun doing so.
	<br><br>
	<b>Signed:</b><br>
	<i>The Gentleman's Club</i>"
	<br><br>
</p>
What an outrageous letter! There's no way you can do stuff like that, is it?<br>
But then again... You'll have to take the hit to your image if you choose to ignore it. And in this town of molesters and rapists, that can't be a good thing.
<br><br>
<span class="italic gold">From now on, you may check what your task is in your journal.</span>
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.blackmail.intro to 1>><<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
<<if $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.includesItems>>
	<<linkreplace "Take contents">>
		You've taken the included items.
		<<run $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.receiveItems()>>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.includesItems to false>>
		<<updatesidebarimg>>
	<</linkreplace>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link "Close" _blackmailReturn>><<set $xchange.blackmail.hasReadLetter to true>><<if _blackmailReturn isnot "Bedroom">><<endevent>><</if>><</link>>
<br>

:: Blackmail Reread Letter
<<set _blackmailHome to $avery_mansion ? "Mansion Bedroom" : "Bedroom">>
You skim over the unimportant stuff and focus only on the task given to you:
<span class="italic">
	<<blackmail-checkquest>>
</span>
<<if $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.includesItems>>
	<<linkreplace "Take contents">>
		You've taken the included items.
		<<run $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.receiveItems()>>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.includesItems to false>>
		<<updatesidebarimg>>
	<</linkreplace>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link "Close" _blackmailHome>><<set $xchange.blackmail.hasReadLetter to true>><</link>>
<br>

:: Blackmail Conclusion Letter
<<run restoreActiveBlackmailQuest()>>
<<set _activeQuest to $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest>>
<<set _blackmailHome to $avery_mansion ? "Mansion Bedroom" : "Bedroom">>
A new envelope appears to have been slid under your door. You dread to read whatever message it contains, but know better than to ignore the words hidden inside.
<br><br>
Steeling your resolve, you open the envelope and read the letter inside:
<<if _activeQuest.cleared and !_activeQuest.failed>>
	<p class="indent-block italic">
		"<b>Marvelous performance</b>, <<underworld_nickname>>!
		<br><br>
		<<if $xchange.blackmail.passedOutRecently>>
			<span class="purple">We're truly sorry about the nature of today's incidents</span>. This was a terrible assault on your personal integrity and security. And we lament you were forced onto such stressful circumstances. 
			<br><br>
			However, these events, even though abominable to any normal person, are nothing but the will of our <span class="elk">wise master</span>. And must therefore be embraced wholeheartedly. It is not our place to intervene against our master's plan.
			<br><br>			
			That said...
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		<span class="green">Our people have been singing your praises.</span> They really were pleased with the exquisite material we managed to produce in partnership with you. <<if $xchange.blackmail.hasGenderswappedRecently>>In particular, your recent transformation was especially titillating for them. <</if>>You could even say they've been licking their lips in delight ever since. Truly outstanding.
		<br><br>
		<<if penaltyFameSum() lt 1000 or $xchange.blackmail.questsCompleted lt 5>>
			Since you've oh-so gracefully complied with our humble request, we've taken the liberty to include your payment within this very same envelope for the amount of <<moneyGainDisplay `getStaticQuestData(_activeQuest).reward() / 100`>>.
			<<run delete V.xchange.blackmail.paymentsRemoved>>
			<br><br>
		<<elseif !$xchange.blackmail.paymentsRemoved>>
			We believe you've really come to enjoy our tasks, <<underworld_nickname>>. And therefore, <span class="purple">we've concluded paying you for them is no longer necessary.</span> But do keep in mind we'll still be forced to take action should you refuse to comply with future requests as a reprisal.
			<<earnFeat "How They Get You">>
			<<earnFeat "They Got You">>
			<<set $xchange.blackmail.paymentsRemoved to 1>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		Please enjoy the rest of your day. We'll be in touch.
		<br><br>
		<b>Signed:</b><br>
		<i>The Gentleman's Club</i>"
		<br><br>
	</p>
	<<blackmail-endquest>>
	<<if !$xchange.blackmail.paymentsRemoved>>
		<<earnFeat "How They Get You">>
		<<link "Take money and discard the envelope" _blackmailHome>>
			<<moneyGain `getStaticQuestData(_activeQuest).reward() / 100`>>
		<</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link "Discard" _blackmailHome>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<p class="indent-block italic">
		"<b>We're very disappointed</b>, <<underworld_nickname>>.
		<br><br>
		<<if _activeQuest.failed>>
			<<print _activeQuest.failMessage()>>
		<<else>>
			"You've chosen to disregard our reasonable demands.
		<</if>>
		And so, you've left us no other choice than to dock your payment, and release your material out into the world.
		<br><br>
		<span class="red">All actions have consequences.</span><br>
		Please forgive us. But there just was no other way...
		<br><br>
		<b>Signed:</b><br>
		<i>The Gentleman's Club</i>"
		<br><br>
	</p>
	<<blackmail-endquest>>
	<<link "Discard" _blackmailHome>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Bedroom Blackmail Notice
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 0>>
	As you leave the comfort of your bed, suddenly you spot an undescript envelope laying on the floor by your room's door. You can only guess that it must have either been slid under the door while you slept, or you somehow missed it before heading to bed. There's no way anyone entered to leave it there while you slept, is there?
	<br><br>
	Either way, you ponder whether you should inspect such a suspicious item or not.
	<br><br> 	
	Curiosity is getting to you bad. Yet you're not sure that looking inside is such a prudent course of action. This is no spy movie. But the envelope could certainly contain something dangerous. Or perhaps it could be some very juicy gossip...
	<br><br>
	There really is no way to know unless you risk it. <span class="gold">Will you risk it?</span>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	As you leave the comfort of your bed, you spot a familiar-looking envelope. You know this instintively, <span class="purple">it's from  "the Gentleman's Club"</span>. Once again you're unsure as to how or when it got there. Yet you still ponder whether you should indulge them, or simply just ignore the blasted thing, consequences be damned. 
	<br><br>
	Either way, this thing can only spell trouble for you. Though you feel as though you have very little choice on the matter regardless.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Open|Blackmail Letter]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ignore|Bedroom]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Blackmail Great Hawk Delivery
<<endevent>><<effects>><<npc "Great Hawk">>
A sharp cry draws your attention to the moor. A stranger is picking their way towards the tower, but the Great Hawk has already seen them. <<bHe>> dives, talons spread. The stranger turns and flees, abandoning an envelope in the grass.
<br><br>
The Great Hawk returns with the envelope clutched carefully in <<bhis>> talons and sets it before you.
<<if $monster is 1>>
	"Stranger tried to leave this," <<bhe>> says. "Looks valuable. For <<wife>>."
<<else>>
	<<bHe>> taps the envelope, then gestures towards you with a pleased chirp. <<bHe>> seems to think <<bhe>> has brought you something valuable.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Your name is written across the front.
<br><br>
<<blackmail-courier-destroyroll>>
<<if $xchange.blackmail.courierDestroyed>>
	Before you can even take it from <<bhim>>, <<bhe>> loses patience and tears into the envelope <<bhimself>>, shredding it to ribbons in search of something to eat.
	<br><br>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.cooldown to 7>>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
	<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 0>>
		Whatever the stranger wanted from you is now scattered across the moor in scraps. <span class="green">The Great Hawk has saved you from it for now.</span>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
		<<blackmail-resetcourier>>
	<<else>>
		You catch a glimpse of the signature before it's shredded beyond recognition. <span class="red">It was from the Gentleman's Club.</span> Your stomach twists. You have no way to know what they demanded this time, much less how to satisfy them. You're certain they'll make you pay for it.
		<<silently>><<blackmail-newquest>><</silently>>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.letterDestroyed to true>>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.failed to true>>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.effectmessage to 3>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Bird Tower]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Open it|Blackmail Letter]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Blackmail Wolf Delivery
<<effects>>
The pack suddenly bristles and growls towards the cave mouth. A stranger stands in the clearing, an envelope in hand. The <<wolf_cave_plural>> charge, chasing them back into the forest.
<br><br>
One of the <<wolf_cave_plural>> returns with the abandoned envelope between its teeth and drops it at your feet. It's a little crumpled and wet with <span class="lewd">wolf saliva</span>, but your name and the writing inside remain readable.
<br><br>
<<blackmail-courier-destroyroll>>
<<if $xchange.blackmail.courierDestroyed>>
	Before you can pick it up, the <<wolf_cave_plural>> pounce, and the envelope disappears in a flurry of teeth and paws. By the time they lose interest, it's little more than damp, shredded paper.
	<br><br>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.cooldown to 7>>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
	<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 0>>
		You wonder what the letter said, but there's nothing left to read now. Whatever the stranger wanted from you, <span class="green">the pack has saved you from it for now.</span>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
		<<blackmail-resetcourier>>
	<<else>>
		You catch a glimpse of the signature in the wreckage before it's torn apart entirely. <span class="red">It was from the Gentleman's Club.</span> Your stomach twists. You have no way to know what they demanded this time, much less how to satisfy them. You're certain they'll make you pay for it.
		<<silently>><<blackmail-newquest>><</silently>>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.letterDestroyed to true>>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.failed to true>>
		<<set $xchange.blackmail.effectmessage to 3>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Wolf Cave]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Open it|Blackmail Letter]]>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Blackmail Eden Delivery
<<endevent>><<effects>>
<<npc Eden>><<person1>>
Eden abruptly reaches for <<his>> rifle and turns towards the window. A stranger stands near the edge of the clearing. <<He>> shoulders the gun, but the stranger drops an envelope and retreats into the forest before <<he>> can take aim.
<br><br>
Eden retrieves the envelope and tears it open. <<His>> expression darkens as <<he>> reads. "I hate this kind of shit," <<he>> growls. "City people. Always hiding behind paper and pretty words." <<He>> tears the letter into strips and throws them into the fire, continuing to grumble about the people in town.
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.blackmail.cooldown to 7>>
<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 0>>
	You wonder what the letter said, but Eden refuses to repeat it. Whatever the stranger wanted from you, <span class="green">Eden has saved you from it for now.</span>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
	<<blackmail-resetcourier>>
<<else>>
	You recognised the signature before Eden destroyed it. <span class="red">It was from the Gentleman's Club.</span> Your stomach twists. You have no way to know what they demanded this time, much less how to satisfy them. You're certain they'll make you pay for it.
	<<silently>><<blackmail-newquest>><</silently>>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.letterDestroyed to true>>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest.failed to true>>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.effectmessage to 3>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Eden Cabin]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Blackmail Avery Mansion Cover
<<endevent>>
<<npc "Avery">><<person1>>
You're still getting your bearings when you notice <<him>> holding an envelope, turning it over in <<his>> hands. Your name is written across the front in that same hurried scrawl you've come to dread.
<br><br>
<<He>> tears it open before you can say anything, scans the contents, and <<his>> expression darkens. "Absolute vultures," <<he>> mutters, almost to <<himself>>. Without another word, <<he>> folds the letter and its photographs back into the envelope and feeds the whole thing into the nearest fireplace.
<br><br>
"You don't need people like that circling you," <<he>> says, watching it burn. "Not while I'm around."
<br><br>
<span class="green">Avery has saved you from it, for now.</span>
<br>
<<set $xchange.blackmail.cooldown to 7>>
<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
<<blackmail-resetcourier>>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Blackmail Avery Mansion Decline
/* Fragment only */
<<endevent>>
<<npc "Avery">><<person1>>
<<He>> notices the envelope on the floor before you do, and picks it up. <<His>> eyes flick over your name written across the front, and something shifts behind <<his>> expression. <<He>> turns it over once, then thinks better of opening it, and sets it back down within your reach.
<br><br>
"Whatever this is," <<he>> says carefully, "I'd rather not know." <<He>> straightens <<his>> collar. "People already talk enough about this house as it is."
<br><br>

:: Blackmail Temple Delivery
<<endevent>><<effects>>
<<generate1>><<person1>><<npc "Jordan" 2>><<person2>>
Jordan is speaking with a finely dressed <<person1>><<person>> in a dark suit. The stranger notices you and smiles. Jordan follows <<person1>><<his>> gaze, notices you too, and smiles.
<br><br>
"Please excuse me," the stranger says. Jordan nods, and the <<person1>><<person>> passes <<person2>><<him>> a sealed envelope before walking away.
<br><br>
"That fine <<person1>><<gentleman_npc>> wanted me to give you this," Jordan says, offering you the envelope. Your name is written across the front. <<person2>><<He>> looks as though <<he>> wants to ask you something, but the <<bishop_hands>> turn towards <<him>>.
<br>
"Do not become too emotional."
<br>
"Remember your composure."
<br><br>
Jordan lowers <<his>> head. "Of course." <<He>> leaves you to read the letter alone.
<br><br>
<<link [[Open it|Blackmail Letter]]>><<set $phase to 4>><</link>>
<br>

:: Blackmail Poppy Delivery
<<endevent>><<effects>>
<<npc Poppy>><<person1>>
<<if Number(C.npc.Poppy.patience) lt 10>>
	You spot an envelope that's been slipped under the door. Poppy notices it too, glances at your name scrawled across the front, and looks away without a word, <<his>> mouth set in a thin, irritated line. Whatever it is, <<he>> clearly can't be bothered with it right now.
	<br><br>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.courier to "home">>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.courierAfk to true>>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.courierReady to false>>
	<<link [[Next|Flats Poppy Living Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You spot an envelope that's been slipped under the door before Poppy does, but <<he>> gets to it first, scooping it up and turning it over in <<his>> hands. Your name is written across the front in that same hurried scrawl.
	<br><br>
	<<His>> brow furrows. "Wait a minute," <<he>> says, already peeling back the flap. "Let me see this first."
	<br><br>
	You watch <<his>> face as <<he>> reads. Whatever playfulness was there a moment ago drains away, replaced by something gloomier, <<his>> eyes flicking back and forth over the page.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> folds the letter and its photographs back into the envelope without a word, tucking it away out of your reach. "I know someone who can make this kind of trash disappear," <<he>> says at last, <<his>> voice steadier than <<his>> expression. "You don't need to worry about it. Rest assured."
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">Poppy has saved you from it, for now.</span>
	<br>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.cooldown to 7>>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
	<<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
	<<blackmail-resetcourier>>
	<<link [[Next|Flats Poppy Living Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
